l_english:

 vladwyn_canon.1000.t:0 "Among Dragons and Lanterns"
 vladwyn_canon.1000.desc:0 "The celebrations for Rhaenyra and Laenor fill the hall with music, wine and enough silk to ransom a minor lord.\n\nTristan has spent most of the evening where I expected to find him: watching doors, judging swordsmen and looking profoundly unimpressed by noble pageantry.\n\nUntil, that is, his attention settles upon Elyse Sunglass.\n\nTheir first conversation is brief. Then comes another. And by the time the musicians begin their next song, my old friend appears to have discovered something at court more dangerous than any blade."
 vladwyn_canon.1000.a:0 "So the Black Sentinel has finally lowered his guard."


 vladwyn_canon.1010.t:0 "A Vladwyn and a Sunglass"
 vladwyn_canon.1010.desc:0 "What began beneath the lights of a royal celebration has become something neither Tristan nor Elyse seems interested in hiding.\n\nThere is no great political design behind it. No kingdom to inherit. No lord paramount bargaining across a painted table.\n\nTristan wants her. Elyse wants him.\n\nFor a man who has spent so much of his life carrying steel for others, it is perhaps fitting that the choice he makes for himself should be so simple."
 vladwyn_canon.1010.a:0 "Then let them build a life together."


 vladwyn_canon.1020.t:0 "The Light Goes Out"
 vladwyn_canon.1020.desc:0 "Elyse Sunglass is dead.\n\nThere are wounds Tristan understands. A sword leaves a mark. An arrow can be pulled free. Even defeat gives a warrior something tangible to hate.\n\nThis gives him nothing.\n\nHe has his children. He has his name. He has men who would follow him into battle without hesitation.\n\nBut when I speak to him of the years still ahead, Tristan's answer is quiet and final.\n\nThere will never be another wife."
 vladwyn_canon.1020.a:0 "Then I will not ask him to forget her."


 vladwyn_canon.1030.t:0 "The Princess's Sword"
 vladwyn_canon.1030.desc:0 "Dragonstone has found a use for Tristan's grief.\n\nPrincess Rhaenyra has asked him to remain at her side, not merely as another warrior at court, but as the man responsible for sharpening those around her.\n\nMaster-at-arms. Captain of her household guard. Her sworn sword when steel is required and ceremony is not.\n\nI have known Tristan long enough to recognize purpose when it returns to his eyes.\n\nHe will leave my court for hers.\n\nI cannot begrudge him that."
 vladwyn_canon.1030.a:0 "Rhaenyra could choose no better sword."


 vladwyn_canon.1040.t:0 "The Black Sentinel"
 vladwyn_canon.1040.desc:0 "The realm has divided itself between crowns.\n\nRhaenyra now gathers around her those whose loyalty is not merely written in oaths but proven in blood.\n\nAmong them stands Tristan Vladwyn.\n\nShe names him Lord Commander of her own guard, the shield of the Black Queen and the sword entrusted with the lives of those closest to her.\n\nMen have begun calling him the Black Sentinel.\n\nFor once, the name fits before the song has even been written."
 vladwyn_canon.1040.a:0 "Then let the Black Queen have her Sentinel."


 vladwyn_canon.1050.t:0 "The White Cloak"
 vladwyn_canon.1050.desc:0 "The war has ended, but King's Landing has not remembered how to breathe.\n\nA boy sits the Iron Throne. The city is exhausted. Old loyalties remain dangerous, new loyalties remain untested, and every corridor of the Red Keep seems to contain the ghost of someone who expected to rule it.\n\nAegon III needs men whose word has already survived a civil war.\n\nTristan is summoned once more.\n\nThis time there is no separate black guard and no rival crown. He takes the white cloak as Lord Commander of the Kingsguard itself.\n\nAlongside Cregan Stark and me, the Black Sentinel now faces a task stranger than war: putting a kingdom back in order."
 vladwyn_canon.1050.a:0 "We survived the war. Now we rebuild the realm."